# Repository-declared line-ending policy (change 298).
#
# Git normalises text files to LF in the index and checks them out with LF in
# every working tree, so a fresh clone of the same commit produces byte-identical
# text files on Linux, macOS and Windows. This removes the platform dependency
# that previously let source-text assertions pass on CI and fail on a Windows
# checkout.
#
# Binary artifacts are declared explicitly so Git never transforms their bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
